Alternative for PS-API-5: leave graphCheck() unchanged (no allocation in
a Check routine) and instead make each label consumer robust. Example:
SCOTCH_graphTabLoad() already sorts graph labels; bound the merge so a
duplicate graph label cannot assign a wrong part. Does not stop every
other label consumer misbehaving, and does not surface the invalid graph
to the user.

--- a/src/libscotch/library_graph_map_io.c
+++ b/src/libscotch/library_graph_map_io.c
@@ -160,6 +160,9 @@
     if (vertsortflag != 1)                        /* If graph label data not sorted     */
       intSort2asc1 (vertsorttab, vertnbr);        /* Sort sort area by ascending labels */
+    for (vertsortnum = 1; vertsortnum < vertnbr; vertsortnum ++)
+      if (vertsorttab[vertsortnum].labl == vertsorttab[vertsortnum - 1].labl)
+        break;                                    /* Duplicate graph label: left to caller */
 
     for (vertsortnum = 0, mappfilenum = 0; vertsortnum < vertnbr; vertsortnum ++) {
